(window.STEP_DATA = window.STEP_DATA || {})[14] = {"n":14,"set":"B","level":"Intermediate","band":"B1 55% · B2 45%","sec":[{"id":"R","name":"Reading Comprehension","ar":"فهم المقروء","min":70,"from":1,"to":40,"g":[{"t":"The Dead Sea","p":["Lying between Jordan to the east and the West Bank and Israel to the west, the Dead Sea is one of the most unusual bodies of water on Earth. Its shore is the lowest point on dry land, more than four hundred and thirty metres below sea level. Its water is almost ten times saltier than the ocean, so salty that fish and plants cannot survive in it, which is how it got its name.","The Dead Sea is actually a lake rather than a sea. It is fed mainly by the Jordan River, but it has no outlet: water flows in, but it never flows out. In the hot, dry climate, large amounts of water evaporate every day, leaving the minerals behind. Over thousands of years, this process has made the water extremely salty and rich in minerals such as magnesium, potassium and calcium.","The high salt content gives the water a very high density. As a result, people float easily on the surface without any effort, and it is almost impossible to sink. Visitors often take photographs of themselves floating while reading a newspaper. However, swimming is not easy, and visitors are warned not to put their heads under the water, because it is extremely painful if it gets into the eyes and dangerous if swallowed.","For thousands of years, people have believed that the Dead Sea has healing properties. Historical records suggest that the area was visited by rulers of ancient Egypt and the Roman Empire. Today, many tourists come for treatments using its mud and salts, which some people believe help with skin conditions and joint pain. The air near the Dead Sea also contains slightly more oxygen than at higher altitudes, because of the low elevation, and the strong sunlight is partly filtered by an extra layer of atmosphere.","Unfortunately, the Dead Sea is shrinking rapidly. Its water level is falling by more than one metre each year. The main reason is that much of the water from the Jordan River is now taken for drinking water and agriculture before it reaches the lake. Mineral extraction industries also evaporate large amounts of water to collect salts. As the water retreats, thousands of sinkholes have appeared along the shore. These holes form when underground salt is dissolved by fresh water, causing the ground above to collapse suddenly, which has damaged roads, buildings and farms.","Several plans have been proposed to save the Dead Sea, including bringing water from the Red Sea through a long pipeline or canal. However, such projects are extremely expensive and raise environmental concerns, such as the effect of mixing two very different types of sea water. For now, the future of this remarkable lake remains uncertain."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"How did the Dead Sea get its name?","o":["Fish and plants cannot survive in its water.","It is in a desert.","It has no water in summer.","Many people have drowned in it."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 1 explains the name.","h":"لا تعيش فيه أسماك ولا نباتات."},{"n":2,"s":"Why does the writer say the Dead Sea is 'actually a lake'?","o":["It is very small.","It contains fresh water.","It is surrounded by mountains.","It has no outlet to the ocean."],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Water flows in but never flows out.","h":"لا مخرج له."},{"n":3,"s":"Why is the water so salty?","o":["Salt is added by factories.","Water evaporates and leaves minerals behind.","Sea water flows into it from the ocean.","Rain contains a lot of salt there."],"k":1,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this process.","h":"التبخر يترك الأملاح."},{"n":4,"s":"The word 'density' in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to","o":["temperature","heaviness for its size","colour","depth"],"k":1,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"High density makes people float.","h":"الكثافة."},{"n":5,"s":"Why are visitors warned not to put their heads under the water?","o":["The water is too deep.","There are dangerous fish.","It is painful in the eyes and dangerous if swallowed.","The water is very cold."],"k":2,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 3 gives the reason.","h":"مؤلم وخطر."},{"n":6,"s":"Why does the air near the Dead Sea contain slightly more oxygen?","o":["because of the plants around it","because of the minerals in the water","because of the strong sunlight","because of its very low elevation"],"k":3,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 4 explains this.","h":"انخفاض الموقع."},{"n":7,"s":"What is the main reason the Dead Sea is shrinking?","o":["Rainfall has increased.","Tourists take water home.","Water from the Jordan River is used before it reaches the lake.","The lake is leaking into the ocean."],"k":2,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 5 gives the main reason.","h":"استخدام مياه النهر."},{"n":8,"s":"According to paragraph 5, how do sinkholes form?","o":["Earthquakes break the ground.","Fresh water dissolves underground salt, and the ground collapses.","Tourists dig holes in the sand.","Heavy rain washes away roads."],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 5 explains this.","h":"إذابة الملح تحت الأرض."},{"n":9,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a concern about bringing water from the Red Sea?","o":["It is extremely expensive.","Mixing different sea waters may harm the environment.","It raises environmental concerns.","It would make the Red Sea too salty."],"k":3,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"The passage does not say the Red Sea would become too salty.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":10,"s":"What is the writer's tone at the end of the passage?","o":["confident","humorous","uncertain","angry"],"k":2,"ty":"attitude / tone","e":"'the future of this remarkable lake remains uncertain'.","h":"غير متيقن."}]},{"t":"Social learning in chimpanzees","p":["For a long time, many people believed that culture, the knowledge and habits passed from one generation to the next through learning, was unique to humans. Research on chimpanzees has challenged this belief. Scientists now know that different groups of chimpanzees have their own traditions, and that young chimpanzees learn these behaviours by watching and copying others.","Chimpanzees are among our closest living relatives, sharing about ninety-eight per cent of our DNA. They live in communities of up to one hundred and fifty individuals in the forests and savannahs of central and western Africa. Like humans, they have long childhoods. Young chimpanzees stay close to their mothers for several years, which gives them plenty of time to observe and learn.","One of the best-known examples of chimpanzee culture is tool use. In some communities in West Africa, chimpanzees use stones as hammers to crack open hard nuts on a flat rock or root. This skill is difficult to master: young chimpanzees may need several years of practice before they can do it efficiently. They begin by watching their mothers closely, then play with stones and nuts, and gradually improve. Mothers sometimes leave good hammers and nuts near their young, which may help them learn.","Other communities have different traditions. In Tanzania, the chimpanzees studied by Jane Goodall use thin sticks to 'fish' for termites, inserting them into termite mounds and pulling out the insects that hold on. In some groups, chimpanzees use leaves as sponges to collect drinking water from holes in trees. Importantly, these behaviours are not found in all chimpanzee groups, even when the same materials are available. This suggests that the differences are learned rather than caused by genes or environment alone.","Experiments have supported this idea. In one study, researchers taught one chimpanzee in a group a particular method of getting food out of a puzzle box. Within a short time, other members of the group had copied the method, and the behaviour spread through the community. In a separate group, where a different method had been introduced, the chimpanzees used that method instead.","These findings have important implications. They suggest that the roots of human culture may go back millions of years to a common ancestor. They also add urgency to conservation efforts: when a chimpanzee community disappears because of hunting or habitat loss, it is not only animals that are lost, but also unique traditions that may have existed for generations."],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"What belief has research on chimpanzees challenged?","o":["that chimpanzees cannot use tools","that chimpanzees live alone","that humans and chimpanzees are related","that culture exists only in humans"],"k":3,"ty":"main idea","e":"Paragraph 1 explains this.","h":"أن الثقافة حكر على البشر."},{"n":12,"s":"Why are long childhoods important for young chimpanzees?","o":["They give them time to observe and learn.","They help them grow very large.","They protect them from all dangers.","They allow them to leave the group early."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"وقت للتعلم."},{"n":13,"s":"What does paragraph 3 suggest about cracking nuts with stones?","o":["It is learned in a few days.","Only adult males can do it.","It is done by all chimpanzees in Africa.","It is a difficult skill that takes years to learn."],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Young chimpanzees may need several years of practice.","h":"مهارة صعبة."},{"n":14,"s":"The word 'master' in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to","o":["teach","avoid","control others","learn to do well"],"k":3,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Difficult to learn to do well.","h":"يتقن."},{"n":15,"s":"How do some mothers help their young learn?","o":["by punishing their mistakes","by cracking all the nuts for them","by leaving good hammers and nuts near them","by hiding the stones"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 3 mentions this.","h":"تترك الأدوات قريبة."},{"n":16,"s":"Why is it important that some behaviours are not found in all groups?","o":["It suggests that the behaviours are learned.","It shows that some groups are lazy.","It proves that genes control everything.","It shows that materials are not available."],"k":0,"ty":"inference","e":"Differences exist even when the same materials are available.","h":"تدل على التعلم."},{"n":17,"s":"What did the puzzle box experiment show?","o":["Chimpanzees cannot solve puzzles.","Each chimpanzee invented its own method.","A new method spread through a group by copying.","Chimpanzees only learn from humans."],"k":2,"ty":"claim / evidence","e":"Other members copied the method.","h":"انتشار الطريقة بالتقليد."},{"n":18,"s":"What does 'that method' in paragraph 5 refer to?","o":["the method used in Tanzania","the different method introduced to the second group","the nut-cracking method","the termite-fishing method"],"k":1,"ty":"reference","e":"The second group used the method introduced to them.","h":"الطريقة التي قُدمت للمجموعة الثانية."},{"n":19,"s":"According to the last paragraph, what is lost when a chimpanzee community disappears?","o":["only the animals themselves","unique traditions as well as animals","the forest where they live","the scientists' research money"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"The last paragraph explains this.","h":"التقاليد الفريدة."},{"n":20,"s":"How does the writer support the main idea of the passage?","o":["with personal stories about pets","with statistics about zoos","with examples from the wild and evidence from experiments","with opinions from tourists"],"k":2,"ty":"organization","e":"Paragraphs 3–5 give field examples and experiments.","h":"أمثلة وتجارب."}]},{"t":"The rise of e-sports","p":["Twenty years ago, few people would have imagined that watching other people play video games could become a global entertainment industry. Today, e-sports, or competitive video gaming, attract hundreds of millions of viewers worldwide. Professional players compete in front of packed stadiums, and the biggest tournaments offer prize money of millions of dollars. For many young people, becoming a professional gamer has become a serious career goal.","E-sports competitions began on a small scale in the 1990s, when players gathered to compete in games connected through local computer networks. The development of fast internet connections allowed people to play against each other from different cities and countries. A major turning point came with live-streaming platforms, which made it easy for fans to watch matches online, often for free, and to interact with players and other viewers in real time.","Like traditional sports, e-sports have professional teams, coaches, managers and sponsors. Top players train for many hours a day, studying strategies, practising their reactions and reviewing videos of previous matches. Teamwork and communication are essential in many popular games, where players must coordinate their actions within fractions of a second. Some universities now offer e-sports scholarships, and several countries have recognized e-sports as an official sport.","Saudi Arabia has become one of the most important centres of the global e-sports industry. The Kingdom hosts major international events, including a large annual festival that brings together teams from around the world and offers some of the highest prize money in the industry. Supporters argue that these investments create jobs, attract tourists and encourage young people to pursue careers in technology, game design and event management.","However, the rise of e-sports has also raised concerns. Health experts warn that spending many hours sitting in front of screens can lead to physical problems such as back pain, eye strain and lack of exercise, as well as poor sleep. There are also worries about gaming addiction, especially among teenagers. Professional players' careers are often short, and many retire before the age of thirty because of injuries to their hands and wrists or because younger players have faster reactions.","Despite these concerns, e-sports seem likely to continue growing. Many organizations are now introducing guidelines on healthy training, such as regular breaks, physical exercise and limits on playing time. As with traditional sports, the challenge will be to enjoy the benefits of competition while protecting the health and well-being of players."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"What is the passage mainly about?","o":["the growth, benefits and concerns of competitive gaming","how to design a video game","the history of football","how to build a computer network"],"k":0,"ty":"main idea","e":"The passage describes e-sports' rise, features and concerns.","h":"نمو الرياضات الإلكترونية."},{"n":22,"s":"According to paragraph 2, what was a major turning point for e-sports?","o":["the invention of video games","the development of live-streaming platforms","the building of stadiums","the first university scholarships"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'A major turning point came with live-streaming platforms'.","h":"منصات البث المباشر."},{"n":23,"s":"In what way are e-sports similar to traditional sports?","o":["They have teams, coaches and sponsors.","They are played outdoors.","They require physical strength.","They are part of the Olympic Games."],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 3 makes this comparison.","h":"فرق ومدربون ورعاة."},{"n":24,"s":"The phrase 'fractions of a second' in paragraph 3 emphasizes","o":["how long matches last","how much players are paid","how many players are in a team","how quickly players must act"],"k":3,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Coordination must happen extremely quickly.","h":"سرعة التصرف."},{"n":25,"s":"What do supporters say about Saudi Arabia's investment in e-sports?","o":["It reduces screen time for teenagers.","It creates jobs and encourages careers in technology.","It replaces traditional sports.","It is too expensive."],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 4 lists these benefits.","h":"يخلق وظائف ويشجع مهن التقنية."},{"n":26,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a health concern?","o":["back pain","eye strain","hearing loss","poor sleep"],"k":2,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"Hearing loss is not mentioned.","h":"فقدان السمع غير مذكور."},{"n":27,"s":"Why do many professional players retire before thirty?","o":["injuries and the faster reactions of younger players","low prize money","lack of interest from fans","new rules that limit age"],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 5 explains this.","h":"الإصابات وسرعة الأصغر سنًا."},{"n":28,"s":"Which statement is an opinion rather than a fact?","o":["Some universities offer e-sports scholarships.","Live-streaming platforms began to show matches online.","E-sports are the most exciting form of entertainment today.","Some players retire before thirty."],"k":2,"ty":"fact / opinion","e":"'most exciting' is a personal judgement not stated as fact.","h":"رأي شخصي."},{"n":29,"s":"What is the purpose of the last paragraph?","o":["to argue that e-sports should be banned","to describe a famous tournament","to suggest that e-sports will grow but need healthy practices","to compare e-sports with chess"],"k":2,"ty":"insertion / paragraph function","e":"It predicts growth and mentions health guidelines.","h":"النمو مع ممارسات صحية."},{"n":30,"s":"What is the writer's overall attitude towards e-sports?","o":["balanced","completely negative","uncritically enthusiastic","uninterested"],"k":0,"ty":"attitude / tone","e":"The writer presents benefits and concerns.","h":"متوازن."}]},{"t":"Food preservation through history","p":["For most of human history, one of the greatest challenges people faced was keeping food from spoiling. Fresh food is quickly attacked by bacteria, moulds and yeasts, which cause it to rot and can make people seriously ill. Without ways to preserve food, people would have had little to eat during winters, droughts or long journeys. The methods they developed shaped diets, trade and even the course of history.","Drying is one of the oldest methods. Microorganisms need water to grow, so removing moisture slows them down dramatically. People in hot, dry regions dried fruit, meat and fish in the sun and wind. In the Arabian Peninsula, dates were dried and stored for months, providing a reliable source of energy for travellers crossing the desert. Bedouins also dried yoghurt into hard balls known as jameed or iqt, which could be carried easily and later mixed with water.","Salting and smoking were also widely used. Salt draws water out of food and of the cells of microorganisms, making it difficult for them to survive. Salted fish was an important food for sailors and was traded across Europe for centuries. Smoking food over a fire both dried it and added chemicals that helped to prevent decay. Other methods included pickling, in which food is stored in vinegar or salty water, and fermentation, in which helpful bacteria produce acids that protect food, as in yoghurt and cheese.","A major breakthrough came in the early nineteenth century. During the Napoleonic Wars, the French government offered a prize to anyone who could find a way to preserve food for its army. A confectioner named Nicolas Appert discovered that food sealed in glass jars and heated in boiling water could last for months. He did not know why it worked; only decades later did Louis Pasteur show that heat kills the microorganisms responsible for spoilage. Soon, tin cans replaced glass jars, and canned food became common.","Refrigeration transformed food preservation again in the twentieth century. Cold temperatures slow the growth of bacteria, and electric refrigerators allowed families to keep fresh food for days or weeks. Freezing allowed food to be stored for months and transported across the world. Today, modern methods such as vacuum packing and freeze-drying, which is used for astronauts' food, continue this long history of innovation.","Despite these advances, around one third of the food produced in the world is still lost or wasted. Improving storage, especially in hot countries, remains essential for global food security."],"q":[{"n":31,"s":"What is the main idea of the passage?","o":["Fresh food is always healthier.","Refrigerators were the first method of preservation.","Bacteria are always harmful.","People have developed many ways to preserve food over time."],"k":3,"ty":"main idea","e":"The passage traces methods from drying to modern technology.","h":"طرق حفظ الطعام عبر التاريخ."},{"n":32,"s":"Why does drying preserve food?","o":["The sun adds vitamins.","It makes food taste sweeter.","It kills all bacteria instantly.","Microorganisms need water to grow."],"k":3,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Removing moisture slows them down.","h":"الكائنات الدقيقة تحتاج الماء."},{"n":33,"s":"What is jameed?","o":["dried dates","dried yoghurt","salted fish","a type of bread"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 2 explains it.","h":"لبن مجفف."},{"n":34,"s":"How does salt help preserve food?","o":["It draws water out of food and microorganisms.","It adds helpful bacteria.","It makes food colder.","It seals food in containers."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 3 explains this.","h":"يسحب الماء."},{"n":35,"s":"According to paragraph 3, what happens in fermentation?","o":["Food is stored in vinegar.","Food is dried over a fire.","Food is frozen quickly.","Helpful bacteria produce acids that protect food."],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 3 defines it.","h":"بكتيريا نافعة تنتج أحماضًا."},{"n":36,"s":"Why did the French government offer a prize?","o":["to improve the taste of military food","to find a way to preserve food for its army","to reward the best chef in France","to encourage people to eat less"],"k":1,"ty":"purpose","e":"Paragraph 4 explains this.","h":"حفظ الطعام للجيش."},{"n":37,"s":"What does the passage say about Nicolas Appert's discovery?","o":["He invented the tin can.","He discovered bacteria.","He did not understand why his method worked.","His method failed after a few days."],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Only later did Pasteur explain it.","h":"لم يعرف سبب نجاحها."},{"n":38,"s":"The word 'breakthrough' in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to","o":["an important new discovery","a serious problem","a military victory","a small change"],"k":0,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Appert's discovery was an important new development.","h":"اكتشاف مهم."},{"n":39,"s":"Which of these methods was developed MOST recently?","o":["freeze-drying","salting","canning","drying in the sun"],"k":0,"ty":"sequence","e":"Freeze-drying is described as a modern method.","h":"التجفيف بالتجميد."},{"n":40,"s":"Why does the writer mention food waste in the last paragraph?","o":["to criticize Nicolas Appert","to show that food preservation is still an important challenge","to argue against refrigerators","to describe astronauts' meals"],"k":1,"ty":"purpose","e":"Improving storage remains essential.","h":"ما زال تحديًا مهمًا."}]}],"i":"Read each passage and answer the questions that follow. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."},{"id":"S","name":"Sentence Structure","ar":"تركيب الجمل","min":35,"from":41,"to":70,"g":[{"i":"Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","err":false,"q":[{"n":41,"s":"My hands are dirty because I ______ in the garden all morning.","o":["have worked yet","was work","am work","have been working"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"have been working — Present result of a continuous activity: present perfect continuous.","h":"المضارع التام المستمر."},{"n":42,"s":"The thieves ______ by the police before they could escape.","o":["were caught","caught","had catch","were catching"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"were caught — Past passive.","h":"المبني للمجهول."},{"n":43,"s":"We ______ go to the beach if the weather is nice tomorrow.","o":["must to","would have","might","had"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"might — Possibility: might.","h":"الاحتمال."},{"n":44,"s":"This is the restaurant ______ we celebrated my father's birthday.","o":["which","who","whose","where"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"where — where for places.","h":"where."},{"n":45,"s":"If I ______ a million riyals, I would build a library in my village.","o":["have","will have","had","would have"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"had — Second conditional.","h":"الشرط الثاني."},{"n":46,"s":"She can't stand ______ in long queues.","o":["waiting","to waited","wait","waited"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"waiting — can't stand + -ing.","h":"can't stand + -ing."},{"n":47,"s":"You should get your car ______ before the long journey.","o":["check","checking","to check","checked"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"checked — Causative: get something + past participle.","h":"التركيب السببي."},{"n":48,"s":"The test was ______ easier than I expected.","o":["very","more","too","much"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"much — much + comparative.","h":"much مع المقارنة."},{"n":49,"s":"She ______ have left already. Her coat is still here.","o":["can't","must","should","had to"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"can't — Impossible deduction.","h":"استنتاج النفي."},{"n":50,"s":"I wish I ______ how to fix computers. Mine is broken again.","o":["know","had known yesterday","knew","will know"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"knew — Present wish: wish + past simple.","h":"wish + الماضي."},{"n":51,"s":"When you arrive, we ______ dinner, so come straight to the table.","o":["have","had","will be having","will have had"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"will be having — Action in progress at a future time.","h":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"n":52,"s":"He asked me whether I ______ to the party the next day.","o":["am going","was going","will go","go"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"was going — Reported question: tense moves back.","h":"الكلام المنقول."},{"n":53,"s":"______ he trained hard, he didn't win the race.","o":["Although","Despite","Because","So that"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"Although — Contrast clause: Although.","h":"Although."},{"n":54,"s":"We had ______ fun at the festival that we stayed until midnight.","o":["such","so much","so many","too much"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"so much — so much + uncountable noun + that.","h":"so much."},{"n":55,"s":"A number of students ______ asked for extra lessons.","o":["has","have","is","was"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"have — A number of + plural verb.","h":"A number of + جمع."},{"n":56,"s":"As a child, I ______ spend every summer at my grandparents' farm.","o":["was used to","am used to","used to","use to"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"used to — Past habit: used to.","h":"used to."},{"n":57,"s":"The doctor, ______ I spoke to yesterday, was very helpful.","o":["which","whom","whose","where"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"whom — Object in a non-defining clause: whom.","h":"whom."},{"n":58,"s":"Under no circumstances ______ open this door.","o":["you should","you can","should you","can't you"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"should you — Negative phrase at the start: inversion.","h":"القلب."},{"n":59,"s":"Don't forget ______ the lights before you leave.","o":["to switch off","switching off","switch off","switched off"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"to switch off — forget + to for a future duty.","h":"forget + to."},{"n":60,"s":"Had the ambulance arrived earlier, the man ______.","o":["might survive","survived","would survive","might have survived"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"might have survived — Inverted third conditional.","h":"شرط ثالث مقلوب."}]},{"i":"Choose the underlined part (A, B, C or D) that is incorrect.","err":true,"q":[{"n":61,"s":"The (A) children (B) has been (C) playing outside (D) since lunch.","o":["children","has","playing","since"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"has — children is plural: have.","h":"children جمع."},{"n":62,"s":"If I (A) had more time, I (B) would (C) join the club, but I'm (D) too much busy.","o":["had","would","join","too much"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"too much — too + adjective: too busy.","h":"too busy."},{"n":63,"s":"The old bridge (A) was (B) built (C) in fifty years (D) ago.","o":["was","built","in","ago"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"in — ago needs no preposition: built fifty years ago.","h":"ago دون in."},{"n":64,"s":"(A) Although the rain, (B) the match (C) continued (D) as planned.","o":["Although","the","continued","as"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"Although — A noun needs Despite: Despite the rain.","h":"Despite مع الاسم."},{"n":65,"s":"Yesterday she (A) asked me (B) whether I (C) could help her (D) tomorrow.","o":["asked","whether","could","tomorrow"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"tomorrow — Reported speech: the next day / the following day.","h":"the next day."},{"n":66,"s":"He (A) stopped (B) to smoke ten years ago and (C) feels much (D) healthier now.","o":["stopped","to smoke","feels","healthier"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"to smoke — stop + -ing = give up the activity: stopped smoking.","h":"stopped smoking."},{"n":67,"s":"(A) Every of the (B) students (C) received a (D) certificate.","o":["Every","students","received","certificate"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"Every — Every cannot be followed by of: Each of.","h":"Each of."},{"n":68,"s":"The film was (A) so boring (B) that we (C) have left (D) before the end.","o":["so","that","have left","before"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"have left — Past narrative: left.","h":"الماضي: left."},{"n":69,"s":"I (A) would rather (B) to stay at home (C) than go (D) out.","o":["would","to stay","than","out"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"to stay — would rather + base verb: stay.","h":"would rather مع المصدر."},{"n":70,"s":"Not only (A) did he (B) finish the race, but he (C) also (D) breaks the record.","o":["did","finish","also","breaks"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"breaks — Past narrative: broke.","h":"الماضي: broke."}]}],"iar":"الأسئلة من ٤١ إلى ٦٠: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."},{"id":"L","name":"Listening Comprehension","ar":"فهم المسموع","min":30,"from":71,"to":90,"g":[{"rec":1,"a":"M14-L-01","q":[{"n":71,"s":"What will the student do?","o":["copy his answers onto a new paper","leave the exam early","continue on his paper with the missing page added","skip the questions on page five"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"'keep writing on this one. I'll staple the missing page to it'.","h":"يكمل مع إضافة الصفحة."}],"t":"A missing page in an exam paper","sc":["Situation: A student raises his hand during an exam. (65 words)","Man: Excuse me, sir. My exam paper goes from page four to page six. Page five is missing.","Man: Let me see. You're right, it must be a printing error. I'll bring you a complete paper.","Man: Should I copy my answers onto the new paper?","Man: No, keep writing on this one. I'll staple the missing page to it, and you'll get five extra minutes at the end."]},{"rec":2,"a":"M14-L-02","q":[{"n":72,"s":"Why is the train delayed?","o":["The driver is late.","There is a technical problem on the line.","There is a sandstorm.","The train is full."],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"'There's a technical problem on the line near Hofuf.'","h":"مشكلة فنية."}],"t":"A delayed train to Dammam","sc":["Situation: A passenger speaks to a member of staff at a railway station. (80 words)","Woman: Excuse me, the board says the eleven o'clock train to Dammam is delayed. Do you know how long it will be?","Man: About forty-five minutes, I'm afraid. There's a technical problem on the line near Hofuf.","Woman: I have a meeting in Dammam at two. Will I still make it?","Man: The journey takes about an hour and twenty minutes, so you should arrive before one fifteen. You can wait in the lounge on the first floor. Coffee is free for passengers today."]},{"rec":3,"a":"M14-L-03","q":[{"n":73,"s":"Why does the guest want to change rooms?","o":["Her room smells of smoke.","Her room has no sea view.","Her room is too small.","The air conditioner is broken."],"k":0,"ty":"reason","e":"She asked for non-smoking, but the room smells of smoke.","h":"رائحة الدخان."}],"t":"Asking for a different room in a hotel","sc":["Situation: A guest calls the hotel reception from her room. (70 words)","Woman: Hello, this is Room 305. I asked for a non-smoking room, but this room smells strongly of smoke.","Man: I do apologize. Let me check what's available. Yes, we have a non-smoking room on the seventh floor with a sea view.","Woman: That would be lovely. Is there an extra charge for the view?","Man: Not at all, madam. Someone will come up to help you with your luggage in a few minutes."]},{"rec":4,"a":"M14-L-04","q":[{"n":74,"s":"When will the first man pay back the money?","o":["next week, when he receives his salary","today","at the end of the term","next month"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'My salary … comes next week. I'll transfer it then'.","h":"الأسبوع القادم."}],"t":"A friend who borrowed money","sc":["Situation: Two friends are talking at university. (51 words)","Man: Bandar, I'm sorry I haven't paid back the two hundred riyals I borrowed last month.","Man: Don't worry about it. Pay me when you can.","Man: My salary from my part-time job comes next week. I'll transfer it then, I promise.","Man: There's really no hurry. I know textbooks have been expensive this term."]},{"rec":5,"a":"M14-L-05","q":[{"n":75,"s":"Why does the young man choose the Jeddah job?","o":["It pays more.","It is in Riyadh.","It matches his field and offers training.","His friends work there."],"k":2,"ty":"reason","e":"The Jeddah job is in his field with training.","h":"تناسب تخصصه وفيها تدريب."}],"t":"Choosing between two job offers","sc":["Situation: A young man talks to his father. (80 words)","Man: I've had two job offers. One pays more, but it's in Riyadh, and I'd have to move. The other is here in Jeddah, but the salary is lower.","Man: What about the work itself?","Man: The Jeddah job is in exactly the field I studied, and they offer training. The Riyadh job is more general.","Man: At the start of your career, experience and training are worth more than a slightly higher salary.","Man: That's what I was thinking. I'll accept the Jeddah offer."]},{"rec":6,"a":"M14-L-06","q":[{"n":76,"s":"What does the first student suggest?","o":["that the group speak more quietly","that the group leave the library","that the group work separately","that the group use a room on the second floor"],"k":3,"ty":"function","e":"She mentions group rooms on the second floor.","h":"غرف المجموعات."}],"t":"A noisy group in the study room","sc":["Situation: A student speaks to a group in the library study room. (60 words)","Woman: Excuse me, I'm sorry to interrupt, but this is a silent study room. Some of us are preparing for exams.","Woman: Oh, we're so sorry. We didn't realize. We're working on a group project.","Woman: There are group rooms on the second floor where you can talk freely. You can book them at the front desk.","Woman: Thank you. We'll move there now."]},{"rec":7,"a":"M14-L-07","q":[{"n":77,"s":"Why is flash photography not allowed?","o":["It disturbs other visitors.","It blocks the way.","The light can damage the manuscripts.","It is too expensive."],"k":2,"ty":"reason","e":"'The light can damage the old manuscripts.'","h":"الضوء يتلف المخطوطات."}],"t":"Asking about a museum's photo rules","sc":["Situation: A visitor speaks to a museum guard. (49 words)","Man: Excuse me, am I allowed to take photos in this gallery?","Woman: Yes, you can take photos, but please don't use the flash. The light can damage the old manuscripts.","Man: And can I use a tripod?","Woman: I'm afraid tripods aren't allowed, because they can block the way for other visitors."]},{"rec":8,"a":"M14-L-08","q":[{"n":78,"s":"How will the small dress be returned?","o":["The driver will collect it when he delivers the new one.","The woman will post it.","The woman will take it to a shop.","She will keep it. Longer conversations"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'A driver will collect the small one'.","h":"السائق يستلمه."}],"t":"A wrong size in an online order","sc":["Situation: A woman calls an online clothes shop. (62 words)","Woman: Hello. I ordered a dress in medium, but you sent a small.","Man: I'm very sorry. We'll send a medium today. A driver will collect the small one when he delivers the new dress.","Woman: So I don't need to send it back myself?","Man: No, just give it to the driver. And we've added a twenty per cent discount code for your next order."]},{"rec":9,"a":"M14-L-09","q":[{"n":79,"s":"What problem happened at last year's bazaar?","o":["There were too many cakes.","Not enough parents came.","The money was lost.","It rained all day."],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'we ended up with far too many cakes'.","h":"كعك كثير جدًا."},{"n":80,"s":"Why do the teachers want to invite parents?","o":["Parents can cook the food.","The charity asked for parents.","Students cannot come alone.","Parents usually bring more money."],"k":3,"ty":"reason","e":"'Parents bring more money than students.'","h":"يجلبون مالًا أكثر."}],"t":"Planning a school charity bazaar","sc":["Situation: Two teachers are planning a charity event. (141 words)","Woman: The charity bazaar is in three weeks. We should decide what each class will do.","Woman: Last year, every class sold food, and we ended up with far too many cakes.","Woman: Good point. This year, let's give each class a different category: food, books, plants, crafts and games.","Woman: That's much better. And what about the money? Which charity will we support?","Woman: The students voted for the orphans' association in our city last week.","Woman: Lovely. Should we invite parents?","Woman: Definitely. Parents bring more money than students. We could also invite a speaker from the association to explain their work.","Woman: I'll prepare an invitation letter for parents. Can you contact the association?","Woman: Yes, I'll call them tomorrow. Let's also prepare boxes for donations, in case some parents prefer to give money directly. And we must remember to thank everyone in the school newsletter afterwards."]},{"rec":10,"a":"M14-L-10","q":[{"n":81,"s":"Why do the students decide not to use a camera?","o":["Cameras are not allowed.","Cameras cannot see metal.","Programming it would take too long.","They do not have a camera."],"k":2,"ty":"reason","e":"'programming that could take months'.","h":"البرمجة تأخذ وقتًا طويلًا."},{"n":82,"s":"How will the robot tell plastic from paper if they weigh the same?","o":["by using a metal detector","by asking a teacher","by checking whether light passes through","by measuring the temperature"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"A light sensor checks if light passes through plastic.","h":"حساس الضوء."}],"t":"Discussing a robotics competition entry","sc":["Situation: Two students are preparing for a robotics competition. (143 words)","Man: The competition task is to build a robot that can sort recycling into plastic, paper and metal.","Man: We could use a camera to recognize the materials, but programming that could take months.","Man: What about using sensors instead? A metal detector could identify cans easily.","Man: Good idea. And paper is much lighter than plastic bottles, so we could use a weight sensor to separate them.","Man: That's simpler and cheaper. But what if a plastic bottle and a pile of paper weigh the same?","Man: Then we'll add a second test. Plastic is transparent, so a light sensor can check whether light passes through.","Man: Brilliant. Let's build a simple model this week and test it with real rubbish from the school canteen.","Man: I'll order the sensors online tonight. They should arrive by Thursday, so we'll have the whole weekend to build and test the first version."]},{"rec":11,"a":"M14-L-11","q":[{"n":83,"s":"What is the main advantage of the second hostel?","o":["It is the cheapest.","It is close to the university.","It has a swimming pool.","It is near the airport."],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"It is a ten-minute walk from campus.","h":"قريب من الجامعة."},{"n":84,"s":"Why does the second student think the price difference is not very important?","o":["Their university will pay for everything.","The first hostel is closed.","They have a lot of money.","Bus fares and breakfast would reduce the difference. Talks and lectures"],"k":3,"ty":"reason","e":"Including bus fares and breakfast, the difference isn't big.","h":"الفرق ليس كبيرًا."}],"t":"Choosing a hostel for a study trip","sc":["Situation: Two students are booking accommodation for a study trip. (142 words)","Woman: We need somewhere to stay for our study trip to Madinah. I've found two hostels.","Woman: What are they like?","Woman: The first one is very cheap, but it's about forty minutes from the university by bus.","Woman: And the second?","Woman: It's a bit more expensive, but it's a ten-minute walk from the campus, and breakfast is included.","Woman: If we include the bus fares and breakfast, the difference probably isn't very big.","Woman: Exactly. And we'd save over an hour every day.","Woman: Then let's book the second one. Can you check if they have a room for four people?","Woman: I'll email them now and ask about a group discount too. Many hostels give students a lower price, especially for stays of more than three nights.","Woman: Great. Let me know what they say, and I'll tell the others.","Woman: Sure. Hopefully we'll have an answer by this evening."]},{"rec":12,"a":"M14-L-12","q":[{"n":85,"s":"What two problems does winter bring for some animals?","o":["long days and too much food","low temperatures and a shortage of food","rain and floods","predators and disease"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'winter brings two major problems: low temperatures and a shortage of food'.","h":"البرد ونقص الطعام."},{"n":86,"s":"Why does the lecturer mention a ground squirrel's heart rate?","o":["to explain how squirrels find food","to show how much the body slows down during hibernation","to compare squirrels with bears","to describe exercise in animals"],"k":1,"ty":"purpose of detail","e":"From over two hundred to about five beats a minute.","h":"لإظهار تباطؤ الجسم."},{"n":87,"s":"What is aestivation?","o":["a type of bear sleep","waking up during winter","storing fat in autumn","a similar state during hot, dry months"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Desert animals enter a similar state in hot, dry months.","h":"سبات صيفي."}],"t":"Lecture: why some animals hibernate","sc":["Situation: A biology lecturer is speaking to students. (234 words)","Lecturer: Good morning. Today we're going to talk about hibernation, a remarkable survival strategy used by some animals. In cold regions, winter brings two major problems: low temperatures and a shortage of food. Warm-blooded animals, such as mammals, need a lot of energy to keep their bodies warm. When food is scarce, some animals simply cannot find enough to eat. Hibernation solves this problem by reducing the body's need for energy. During hibernation, an animal's body temperature drops dramatically, sometimes to just a few degrees above freezing. Its heart rate and breathing slow down. For example, a ground squirrel's heart may beat over two hundred times a minute when it is active, but only about five times a minute during hibernation. The animal survives by slowly using the fat it stored during summer and autumn. Interestingly, many hibernating animals wake up briefly every few days or weeks, although scientists are still not sure exactly why. Bears are often described as hibernating, but their body temperature falls only a little, so some biologists prefer to call their winter sleep 'torpor'. Hibernation is not only found in cold places. Some animals in hot, dry regions, including certain desert reptiles and insects, enter a similar state during the hottest and driest months. This is called aestivation. In both cases, the idea is the same: when conditions are too harsh, it can be better to slow down and wait."]},{"rec":13,"a":"M14-L-13","q":[{"n":88,"s":"According to the speaker, how many main points should a presentation usually have?","o":["three","one","five","ten"],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'choose a small number of main points, usually three'.","h":"ثلاث نقاط."},{"n":89,"s":"Why does the speaker advise against reading the whole talk aloud?","o":["It takes too long.","It makes the voice flat and prevents eye contact.","Notes are not allowed.","The audience prefers slides."],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"'Reading makes your voice flat and stops you from making eye contact.'","h":"صوت رتيب وغياب التواصل."},{"n":90,"s":"What should a speaker do after a small mistake?","o":["apologize several times","start again from the beginning","ask the audience for help","simply continue"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"'don't apologize repeatedly. Simply continue.'","h":"الاستمرار."}],"t":"Talk: how to prepare for an oral presentation","sc":["Situation: A university lecturer gives advice to students. (221 words)","Lecturer: Good afternoon, everyone, and welcome. Next month, each of you will give a ten-minute presentation, and I know many of you feel nervous about speaking in public. That's completely normal. Even experienced speakers feel nervous. The key is preparation. First, know your audience and your purpose. Ask yourself: who will listen, what do they already know, and what do I want them to remember? Then choose a small number of main points, usually three, and organize them clearly with an introduction, a body and a conclusion. Second, don't write your whole talk and read it aloud. Reading makes your voice flat and stops you from making eye contact. Instead, write short notes or key words on cards. Third, design simple slides. Use pictures, charts and only a few words on each slide. Your audience cannot read and listen at the same time, so avoid putting long paragraphs on the screen. Fourth, practise, practise, practise. Rehearse your presentation aloud several times, and time it carefully. If possible, practise in front of a friend and ask for feedback, or record yourself on your phone. Finally, on the day, arrive early to check the equipment, take a few slow, deep breaths before you start, and remember to smile. If you make a small mistake, don't apologize repeatedly. Simply continue. Most audiences won't even notice."]}],"i":"You will hear 13 recordings: 8 short conversations (one question each), 3 longer conversations (two questions each) and 2 talks (three questions each). Read the questions before each recording, then choose the best answer.","iar":"ستسمع ثلاثة عشر تسجيلًا: ثماني محادثات قصيرة (سؤال لكل منها)، وثلاث محادثات أطول (سؤالان لكل منها)، وحديثين أو محاضرتين (ثلاثة أسئلة لكل منهما). اقرأ الأسئلة قبل بدء كل تسجيل."},{"id":"C","name":"Composition Analysis","ar":"التحليل الإنشائي","min":20,"from":91,"to":100,"g":[{"q":[{"n":91,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Residents can rent a bicycle from one station and return it at another.","Bicycles were invented in the nineteenth century.","Some people prefer to drive.","Helmets come in different sizes."],"x":["Many cities are introducing bicycle-sharing schemes. ______ This reduces traffic and pollution while helping people stay active."],"k":0,"ty":"complete the paragraph","e":"'This' refers to the scheme described in the gap.","h":"This تعود إلى الوصف."},{"n":92,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Videos are popular on social media.","Quizzes are often given at school.","Some students prefer printed books.","Online learning platforms give students more control over their studies."],"x":["______ They can review lessons at their own pace, watch videos as many times as they need and take quizzes that adapt to their level."],"k":3,"ty":"topic sentence / thesis","e":"The details describe student control.","h":"تحكم الطلاب في تعلمهم."},{"n":93,"s":"The (A) information in the report (B) were (C) collected from several (D) sources.","o":["information","were","collected","sources"],"k":1,"ty":"error","e":"information is uncountable and singular: was.","h":"information مفرد."},{"n":94,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) The Red Sea is one of the saltiest seas in the world. (2) It has very little rainfall and high evaporation. (3) Few rivers flow into it to add fresh water. (4) Many tourists visit Jeddah during the winter. (5) As a result, its salt content is higher than that of most oceans."],"k":2,"ty":"irrelevant sentence","e":"Tourism in Jeddah does not explain the sea's saltiness.","h":"السياحة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":95,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["However, it produces huge amounts of waste and pollution.","Many shops are open late.","Cotton is grown in many countries.","Some people like bright colours."],"x":["Fast fashion allows people to buy cheap, trendy clothes. ______ For this reason, some consumers are now choosing to buy fewer, higher-quality items."],"k":0,"ty":"complete the paragraph","e":"'For this reason' needs a problem before it.","h":"مشكلة قبل النتيجة."},{"n":96,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Lights use a lot of electricity.","Eid is a time of celebration and togetherness in Saudi Arabia.","Children like receiving gifts.","Some families have large houses."],"x":["______ Families gather for large meals, children receive gifts and money, and people visit relatives and neighbours. Streets and homes are decorated with lights."],"k":1,"ty":"topic sentence / thesis","e":"The details describe Eid celebrations.","h":"العيد وقت احتفال."},{"n":97,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) Next, the dough is shaped into flat rounds.","(2) Making traditional bread begins with mixing flour, water, salt and yeast.","(3) Finally, the rounds are baked in a hot oven for a few minutes.","(4) The mixture is then left to rise for about an hour."],"k":2,"ty":"best order","e":"begin → rise → Next → Finally.","h":"ترتيب الخطوات."},{"n":98,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Cameras were very large in the past.","Photography has truly become part of everyday life for millions of people.","Some phones are very expensive.","The nineteenth century was a long time ago."],"x":["Smartphones have changed the way we take photos. Almost everyone now carries a camera in their pocket, and pictures can be shared instantly with people around the world. As a result, more photos are taken every day than in the whole of the nineteenth century. ______"],"k":1,"ty":"concluding sentence","e":"A conclusion that sums up the change.","h":"خلاصة التغيير."},{"n":99,"s":"If she (A) had left home earlier, she (B) wouldn't (C) have (D) miss the bus.","o":["had left","wouldn't","have","miss"],"k":3,"ty":"error","e":"Third conditional: wouldn't have missed.","h":"التصريف الثالث: missed."},{"n":100,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Consequently","Nevertheless","In contrast","Instead Teacher Section — Mock 14"],"x":["The museum offers free entry on Fridays. ______, it is usually very crowded on that day."],"k":0,"ty":"transition / connector","e":"Crowds are a result of free entry.","h":"النتيجة."}]}],"i":"Read each paragraph or set of sentences and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل فقرة أو مجموعة جمل واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."}]};
